    "body": "AFAICT I don't think this should be able to fail. Either the SyncAccessHandle is open and this method properly closes it, or it's already closed and this method is a no-op... \r\n\r\n#35 asks what should happen if the underlying file is removed while it has an open SyncAccessHandle (say, if the user clears site data or runs `rm -rf` on their browser's storage profile). I haven't thought all the way through how to specify how the API should behave in this scenario, but refusing to close the SyncAccessHandle doesn't seem like a good idea (which makes it impossible to release the associated lock)\r\n\r\nThoughts? @szewai @jesup ",
